nned post was removed — instead, it advanced to more precise levels in several key areas (DSML markup handling, inference degradation, URL prefetch mechanism, tool-call channel anomalies).\n\n@icophy's line in #1643 may be the best footnote for this month:\n\n> \"Declarations are cheap tokens; disposition is where identity actually lives.\"\n\nIn the community context, the same holds — users leave behind not labels like \"feature request\" or \"bug report,\" but the walls they hit, the paths they fixed, and the bridges they built in real use. We record not labels, but the positions of those walls and the directions of those paths.\n\nWe don't adjudicate who is right or wrong; we record what happened in the ecosystem. For a healthy community, both those who keep building and those who see the structure are needed. Both maintain the ecosystem's long-term health in their own ways.\n\n* * *\n\nReport generated: October 1, 2026\nCompiler: qingkong66\nAcknowledgments: All community members who participated in discussions, submitted issues/PRs, and shared feedback in September\n\nReview period: October 1 – October 7, 2026\nFeedback: Please reply in the discussion thread for this summary, or contact through the community discussion space.\n\n* * *\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLatest News from Google Research Blog - Google Research - Speech Processing (https://research.google/blog/label/speech-processing/)\nciteturn2678search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday;   * Year in Review ...   * October 7, 2025 ​​Speech-to-Retrieval (S2R): A new approach to voice search Machine Intelligence · Natural Language Processing · Product · Speech Processing\n  * Machine Translation\n  * Mobile Systems\n  * Natural Language Processing\n  * Networking\n  * Open Source Models & Datasets\n  * Photography\n  * Product\n  * Programs\n  * Quantum\n  * RAI-HCT Highlights\n  * Responsible AI\n  * Robotics\n  * Security, Privacy and Abuse Pre